# One manifestation of a single unified defect (2026-07-30, see
# doc/08_tracking/bug/jit_run_file_pipeline_gaps_2026-07-30.md sections 9-10):
# a module-level global's raw value is never tag-boxed before flowing into
# print/format under JIT. This fixture's own cross-module "import" shape
# turned out not to be the relevant axis -- see section 9.4: get_helper_y()
# below (a FUNCTION CALL) reads correctly because a function return re-boxes
# the value; the direct HELPER_Y reference in main_entry.spl does not cross
# that boundary, matching the module_global_direct_read_untagged fixture's
# same-file case exactly.
#
# HELPER_Y is a plain LITERAL initializer (not a function call, so this is
# deliberately NOT gap 8's "val from function call" shape) defined in this
# non-entry, imported file.
val HELPER_Y = 99

fn get_helper_y() -> i64:
    HELPER_Y
